From a07d2ce865b999f6a4366362c31c82fc4be6dc31 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Z User <z@container>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 19:55:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] backend: scope the %rax shadow-epoch validator to the x86
 family by target, and enforce the discipline on i686

F1 fix (PR #637 audit): the validator's park/epoch APIs are arch-generic
on the shared CodegenState, and the generic pass layer (generate_module ->
generate_load/store -> generate_copy, remat_indexed_acc_safe) runs for
EVERY target. i686/ARM/RISC-V park via raw set_acc, so their
acc_park_epoch stays frozen at 0 while the epoch moves: i686 emits
%eax-destination lines (classified by the universal dest-last rule), and
RISC-V 'call foo' / 'mul' / 'div' lines hit IMPLICIT_RAX_WRITES
unconditionally on operands (common.rs table check precedes the operand
check) - the audit caught 'call', 'mul'/'div' are the same class. The
first acc_has_verified(has=true) after any such bump would debug_assert
on a perfectly healthy foreign-target compilation. The patch's own doc
claims ('targets never share a CodegenState with an x86-64 function';
'keeps non-x86 lines from inflating the epoch') were factually wrong.

Fix, going one step further than the audit's is_x86_64 gate: the epoch
machinery is now target-SCOPED via a debug-only AsmOutput.rax_epoch_active
flag (default false = inert), enabled by the x86-64 AND i686 constructors.
Foreign ISAs are safe by construction, not by luck. i686 is INCLUDED in
the discipline instead of gated off: its accumulator cache tracks %eax
through the same generic paths (same dead-register exposure class), so
its 13 park sites migrate to park_acc and its 2 consuming probes
(operand_to_eax early-return, operand_to_ecx acc-resident arm) to
acc_has_verified. The classifier's vocabulary already covers the full
i686 AT&T set (pushl quiet via NEVER table, popl/leal/divl/etc. via the
generic rule and implicit table).

Both directions of the gate are pinned by unit tests
(epoch_machinery_is_inert_without_target_opt_in,
target_opt_in_arms_the_classifier); the pre-existing validator tests now
opt in explicitly, documenting the precondition. Full unit suite re-run
with debug-assertions ACTIVE: 3550/3550 - zero violations across the
corpus, dual-arch.
