From 1efa444a4797b877d1a1e389a24d962f73bb217a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Z User <z@container>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 21:36:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] x86: stage D32 call arguments width-exact; guard the
 GNU-ld relief flag behind uname

F4 (PR #637 audit, the two nits):

1. Call-argument staging selected the move form by F32-vs-everything:
   a D32 (4-byte) argument with a fresh XMM home took the F64 branch and
   emitted vmovsd/movapd/movq (8-byte) instead of vmovss/movaps/movd
   (4-byte). Correct - staging is a bit move and the consumer reads only
   the low 32 bits - but one byte wider and it reads garbage lanes no
   consumer can observe. The width selection now matches
   F32|D32 in all three arms (AVX scalar, SSE full-copy, GPR bit-cast),
   keeping the width-exactness doctrine the staging fix introduced.

2. tests/regression/check_peephole_whitespace.sh passed
   -C link-arg=-Wl,--no-keep-memory unconditionally. It is a GNU-ld flag;
   a non-GNU ld rejects it and the gate would read a linker error as a
   test failure. Guarded behind uname -s == Linux (the repository targets
   Linux per BUILDING_LINUX.txt; the guard is portability hygiene).
---
 src/backend/x86/codegen/calls.rs              | 15 ++++++++++++---
 tests/regression/check_peephole_whitespace.sh | 10 +++++++++-
 2 files changed, 21 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/backend/x86/codegen/calls.rs b/src/backend/x86/codegen/calls.rs
